---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Methodology | pregnancydiscriminationcalc.com';
const description = 'How the pregnancy discrimination damages calculator works: Title VII caps, back pay, and punitive damages for PDA violations.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p><em>Reviewed by Riley Chen (RC), Employment &amp; Civil Rights Practice Lead. Updated May 2026.</em></p>
  <h2>Title VII framework</h2><p>Back pay: salary/12 × months lost (uncapped). Compensatory damages (emotional distress): 30% of cap without malice, 60% with malice. Punitive: 0 without malice, 40% of cap with malice. Front pay: 50% of annual salary for termination/constructive discharge. All subject to per-employer-size caps of $50K/$100K/$200K/$300K for combined comp + punitive.</p>
  <h2>Cap application</h2><p>The Title VII damages cap applies to the combined compensatory + punitive award. Back pay and front pay are equitable remedies and are not capped. Attorney fees are separately recoverable by the prevailing plaintiff under 42 U.S.C. § 2000e-5(k).</p>
</BaseLayout>
